# CVE-2021-31799: RDoc's remove_unparseable opened each candidate TAGS file
# through Ruby's receiverless `open`. `Kernel#open` is a private instance
# method mixed into Object, so `open path, mode` is `Kernel.open path, mode`,
# and Ruby documents that method as running the path as a subprocess command
# line whenever its first character is `|`. The file list is gathered with
# Dir.glob over the tree being documented, so a repository containing a file
# named `| touch evil.txt && echo tags` ran that command when rdoc walked it
# (CWE-78). The fixed revision spells the call File.open, the form with no pipe
# behaviour.
#
# The path is filesystem-derived rather than from a labelled source, so this is
# the review direction: the flag names the call for a caller audit, and the
# taint rule stays silent until a source reaches it. The callee.path match is
# exact because `~=` is segment-aware in both directions and would pull in the
# patched `File.open` itself.

test "rank1657: a TAGS candidate opened through bare open can run a piped path"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/rdoc/rdoc.rb
  code
  ```
  class RDoc::RDoc
    ##
    # Removes file extensions known to be unparseable from +files+ and TAGS
    # files for emacs and vim.

    def remove_unparseable files
      files.reject do |file, *|
        file =~ /\.(?:class|eps|erb|scpt\.txt|svg|ttf|yml)$/i or
          (file =~ /tags$/i and
           open(file, 'rb') { |io|
             io.read(100) =~ /\A(\f\n[^,]+,\d+$|!_TAG_)/
           })
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1657: the TAGS check opens the same path through File.open"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/rdoc/rdoc.rb
  code
  ```
  class RDoc::RDoc
    ##
    # Removes file extensions known to be unparseable from +files+ and TAGS
    # files for emacs and vim.

    def remove_unparseable files
      files.reject do |file, *|
        file =~ /\.(?:class|eps|erb|scpt\.txt|svg|ttf|yml)$/i or
          (file =~ /tags$/i and
           File.open(file, 'rb') { |io|
             io.read(100) =~ /\A(\f\n[^,]+,\d+$|!_TAG_)/
           })
      end
    end
  end
  ```
